  "stageId": "1",
  "title": "Guard site-docs section renames with legacy aliases and a no-silent-drop test",
  "goal": "# Guard site-docs section renames with legacy aliases and a no-silent-drop test\n\n## Context\nCase study: KainBain task 68714709-3f50-4e5c-bfa6-bac16a36c393 (docs viewer sidebar regroup, from how-it-works/working-with to four new section ids). The upgrade-safety audit (docs/tasks/68714709-3f50-4e5c-bfa6-bac16a36c393/continueity-failure-20261115-214114.md) reproduced live that api/siteDocs.js readDocFile returned null for old section values, so listDocs returned [] and getDoc returned null on a custom KAINBAIN_SITE_DOCS dir using old frontmatter: custom articles silently vanish on update with no alias, warning, or DEPRECATIONS.md entry. The branch fixed it ad hoc with LEGACY_SECTION_ALIASES plus a deprecation note, but no automated guardrail stops the next rename from repeating the silent drop. All existing API suites passed with the new sections, so tests alone did not catch it.\n\n## Steps\n1. Add a permanent regression test proving listDocs/getDoc on a custom docs dir using retired section ids still resolves (via alias or explicit warn), never silently [].\n2. Add a rename guardrail for DOC_SECTIONS in api/siteDocs.js: removing or renaming a section id without a LEGACY_SECTION_ALIASES entry (or equivalent documented mapping) fails a cheap check with a message naming the retired id.\n3. Document the required rename procedure (alias plus DEPRECATIONS.md entry) where the taxonomy is defined so future agents follow it first time.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A section rename without an alias entry fails the new check, naming the retired id.\n- [ ] Old-section frontmatter still indexes (aliased) with a recorded warning, covered by a regression test.\n- [ ] Valid renames with alias plus deprecation note pass.\n\n## Notes\nStructural follow-on from task 68714709-3f50-4e5c-bfa6-bac16a36c393; see its continuity-failure report and IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md for the full case study. No existing open ticket covers this (checked: binary-safe proof ticket b1c069e0 and flaky-CI quarantine ticket 8769b002 are completed and address different failure modes).",
  "idempotencyKey": "433ab3d7d6e2d7a4d8fa403e0abd8019",
  "execute": false
}' | head -c 1500","description":"Create taxonomy guardrail ticket"}

